    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="0662" n="650" xml:id="pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/2655</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13817</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-11">December 11, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        17.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatches No. 13552
                    of November 26 and No. 13816 of December 11, 1943,<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d597-f1"/> concerning the Brazilian Government’s desire to purchase
                    all of the surplus United States Army engineering and construction equipment in
                    Brazil, I have the honor to transmit herewith a translation of a pertinent
                    letter I have just received from the Foreign Minister.<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d597-f2"/></p>
                <p>This is the letter to which allusion is made in the last paragraph of page 1 of
                    the enclosure to my despatch No. 13552 of November 26; the Brazilian Government
                    is herewith making a formal request for (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) all of
                    the surplus United States Army engineering and construction equipment available
                    in Brazil and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the assignment to Brazil of
                    United States Army engineers to assist in the planning and supervision of a
                    public works program.</p>
                <p>I have sent a translation of the letter to General Walsh.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
